Restore the original WORD league/rank loads in Check_League_Standing @0044c92c.

Literal original instructions: 44c92c mov dx,[0093def4], 44c933 test dx,dx;
44c938 cmp WORD [0093def2],0; 44c94e cmp dx,4;
44c954 cmp WORD [0093def2],3. The two aliases were DWORDs. Reading the
league at def2 also included the rank at def4; reading rank included the
temporary points at def6. Thus bottom-division last place (league=3,rank=4)
returned 3 (relegation) instead of 5 (elimination). The sanctioned patch-834
clamp then concealed this typing error by starting another bottom-division
season instead of returning to the frontend. The unmodified original five-race
Retire/Yes run actually eliminates the player, without decrement or crash.

Both aliases are used only by this function; preserve the original comparisons
and all callers. This also restores winner/promotion/survival classification
when the adjacent temporary-points word is nonzero. No added guard or policy.
